---
// src/pages/terms.astro
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Website Terms | InfraHub"
  description="Terms governing use of the infrahub.tech website. Provider services are governed by the agreement with the selected provider."
  canonicalPath="/terms"
>
  <div class="section section-hero network-overlay">
    <div class="container legal-container">
      <h1 class="legal-title">Website Terms</h1>
      <p class="legal-date">Last Updated: September 2026</p>

      <div class="legal-content">
        <p class="legal-lead">
          These terms govern use of the infrahub.tech website. They do not govern any service supplied to you: partner-delivered services are governed by the agreement with the selected provider, and any direct hardware or supply arrangement by the agreement for that arrangement.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Commercial Role & Scope</h2>
        <p>
          InfraHub provides infrastructure sourcing and advisory services and can introduce prospective buyers to specialist third-party providers across connectivity, cloud, infrastructure, security, and managed operations.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Third-Party Contracting & SLAs</h2>
        <p>
          Unless expressly agreed otherwise in writing for a direct InfraHub supply arrangement, InfraHub is not the underlying carrier, host, cloud operator, security operator, or managed-service provider for partner-delivered services. Provider-specific pricing, service commitments, support terms, and contractual documents are agreed with the selected provider.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Accuracy of Sourcing Information</h2>
        <p>
          Infrastructure availability, hardware stock, routes, capacity, and commercial terms can change. Website content is informational and does not constitute a binding quotation or availability commitment. Any commercial proposal remains subject to confirmation by the relevant supplier or provider and the applicable written agreement.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Intellectual Property</h2>
        <p>
          All trademarks, service marks, and company names referenced on infrahub.tech are the property of their respective owners. Their display does not imply proprietary ownership by InfraHub.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>
          In no event shall InfraHub be liable for any indirect, incidental, consequential, or punitive damages resulting from provider downtime, carrier fiber cuts, hardware supply delays, or third-party SLA failures.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Governing Law</h2>
        <p>
          The contracting entity, governing law, and dispute terms applicable to a commercial engagement are set out in the relevant written agreement. These website terms do not replace the contractual terms agreed for a specific provider or supply arrangement.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-container {
    max-width: 800px;
  }
  .legal-title {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .legal-date {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
  }
  .legal-content {
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
  .legal-content h2 {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin: 32px 0 14px;
  }
  .legal-content p {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
</style>
